## Shadows

Shadows appear only on hover, as lift. Nothing has a resting shadow.

| Variable | Use |
|----------|-----|
| `--shadow-sm` | Small cards (capability cards) |
| `--shadow-md` | Buttons, cursor label |
| `--shadow-lg` | Media (work cards, detail images, hover previews) |

## Layers (z-index)

| Variable | Value | Use |
|----------|-------|-----|
| `--z-raised` | 10 | Marquee bands and their edge fades |
| `--z-nav` | 50 | Fixed nav, hover previews |
| `--z-overlay` | 100 | Mobile menu, skip link, lightbox |
| `--z-cursor` | 200 | Custom cursor label |

In classes: `z-10`, `z-50`, `z-100`, `z-200`. Never `z-[9999]`.

## Breakpoints

Tailwind defaults: `sm` 640, `md` 768, `lg` 1024, `xl` 1280.
- **`lg` is the one layout switch** (the staging About intro still uses `xl` for its two-column story; move it to `lg` when that section is finalised): gutters 32→64, section rhythm 128→192, two-column grids, desktop nav.
- **`sm`** is only for small rearrangements: button rows go horizontal, form fields sit side by side, label sizes step up.
- **`md`** is not used for layout.

## Motion

| Pattern | Values |
|---------|--------|
| Default transition | `--duration-normal` (320ms), `--ease-out-expo` |
| Colour-only change | `--duration-fast` (200ms) |
| Image zoom, media shadow | `--duration-slow` (550ms), `--ease-out-quart`, scale 1.04 |
| Reveal on scroll (`FadeIn`, `ScrollReveal`) | 24px rise and fade, 600ms, `--ease-out-expo`, once |
| Stagger | 80ms steps (`delay={0.08}`, `0.16`). Max 3 steps, inside a list only |
| Hero lines | CSS-only, 100ms steps, so the LCP text never waits for JS |
| Hover lift | Buttons 2px up and press to 98%, arrows 2px up-right, cards 3px up |
| Marquees | 70px per second, all bands. Ease to a stop on hover |
| Count-ups | Start 160ms after entering view, 80ms between numbers |

No bounce or elastic. Every animation has a `prefers-reduced-motion` path: movement off, colour changes kept, count-ups show the final value.

## Icons

lucide-react only, outline at the default stroke.

| Size | Use |
|------|-----|
| 14px | Inside text links and buttons (`cta-arrow`) |
| 18px | UI controls (testimonial arrows, close buttons inline) |
| 24px | Touch-first controls: mobile menu, lightbox |

`ArrowUpRight` means go somewhere. `ArrowDown` means download. Decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`. No emoji.

## Images

| Ratio | Class | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| 16:10 | `aspect-[16/10]` | Work cards, case-study grid images, card motion |
| 16:9 | `aspect-video` | Hero media and video |
| 4:3 | `aspect-[4/3]` | Detail figures and diagrams |
| 21:9 | `aspect-[21/9]` | Wide banners and placeholder panels |
| 1:1 | `aspect-square` | Portrait |

- Media sits on `bg-primary` while loading. Large media uses `rounded-2xl`, small media uses `rounded-lg`.
- Videos are muted, have a poster, and are hidden under reduced motion.
- A replaced image gets a new filename (`-v2`), because `/images/*` is cached for a year.

**Alt text** says what the image shows and why it matters for the case, in sentence case and under 125 characters:
- Name the thing: "SPLT trainer profile and subscription screens".
- Never start with "Image of" or "Picture of".
- No filenames, and no full stop unless there are two sentences.
- Decorative images get `alt=""`.
- Diagrams start with "Diagram:".

## Copy style

### Capitalisation
**Sentence case everywhere:** headings, labels, buttons, nav, categories, service names, page titles and metadata ("Case studies", "What was broken", "Let’s talk", "Brand strategy & identity").

Capitals stay only for:
- proper nouns, brands, places and products (SPLT, Bay Area Trips, Webflow, Amazon);
- **job titles** naming a person’s role (Creative Director, Senior Product Designer, Head of Creative);
- acronyms (UX, UI, CEO);
- the first word after a colon in a credit only when it is a name.

A discipline is lower case ("creative direction"). A title is capped ("Creative Director"). Labels are typed in sentence case and uppercased by CSS, never typed in capitals.

### Numbers
Numbers are proof, so they read as figures.

- **Figures (`8`, `25`, `13`):**
  - every number 10 and over;
  - every number in a stat, fact strip, impact line, card meta, label or table;
  - anything with a unit, %, money, age, page count or date;
  - every number in a sentence that already contains a figure ("from 6 to about 25 in 7 months").
- **Words (one to nine):** only in running prose with no other figure nearby ("Three brand personalities", "two products").
- **"One" meaning "a single"** stays a word ("One listing template"). So do idioms ("a dozen").
- **Sentence starts:** never start a sentence with a figure. Spell the number out or recast the sentence.
- **Approximate and plus:** "about 25", "50+" (no space before +), never "~25".
- **Ranges:** en dash, no spaces: "2–3", "10–12 weeks", "2019–2023".
- **Thousands:** a comma from 1,000 ("4,000"). The decimal mark is a full stop.

### Dates and times (UK)
- **Full date:** "29 October 2026". Day month year, no ordinal, no comma.
- **Meta lines and fact strips:** "Oct 2026". Ranges: "Dec 2024 – Jun 2025" (spaced en dash, because each side has a space). Open-ended: "2024 – present".
- **Years alone:** "2025". Decades: "the 1940s".
- **Time:** 24-hour with a colon, city or zone named for an international reader: "10:00 Cairo time", "15:00 CET". Durations: "24 hours", "7 months".

### Money
- Symbol before the figure, no space: "£8,000", "€500", "$2M".
- Large amounts: `k` and `M`, capital M, no space ("$500k", "$2M").
- Name the currency when the symbol is ambiguous ("A$", "EGP 500", "US$100").

### Units and symbols
- Metric first: "4,000 km", "212 pages", "1,200px". There is a space between the number and the unit, except for `%`, `px`, `°` and `k`/`M`. The number is always bound with `\u00A0` (Tier 6).
- Percent: "12%", "down 23%". Never "percent".
- Use "&" only in labels, categories, service names and credits. Use "and" in sentences.
- Middot `·` with spaces separates meta items and title parts.

### Language
UK English everywhere: colour, organisation, licence (noun), analyse, centre, programme, kilometres. `locale: "en_GB"`, `<html lang="en-GB">`.

